# ── Airtable ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Step 1: Create an Airtable account at airtable.com
#
# Step 2: Create a new Base called "GFA Products"
#
# Step 3: Create a table called "Products" with these exact fields:
#   Name          Short text      (required)
#   Producer      Short text
#   Category      Single select   Options: olive-oils, grains, legumes, snacks, lna, seafood
#   Origin        Short text
#   Description   Long text
#   BuyLinks      Long text       (JSON array — see format below)
#   PillarGood    Long text
#   PillarClean   Long text
#   PillarFair    Long text
#   PillarTrue    Long text
#   Status        Single select   Options: pending, approved, rejected
#   SubmittedBy   Short text
#   EvaluatorNotes Long text
#
# BuyLinks format example:
#   [{"label":"Producer direct","url":"https://producer.com"},{"label":"Amazon","url":"https://amazon.com/..."}]
#
# Step 4: Create a Personal Access Token at airtable.com/create/tokens
#   Scopes needed: data.records:read, data.records:write
#   Access: the "GFA Products" base
#
# Step 5: Get your Base ID from the URL when viewing your base:
#   airtable.com/{BASE_ID}/...  (starts with "app")
#
# Step 6: Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values below:

AIRTABLE_API_KEY=your_personal_access_token_here
AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=appXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
AIRTABLE_TABLE_NAME=Products
